HEIF plug-in for Lumen 1.0
==========================

Lets Lumen import, show, adjust and export HEIF photos (.heic, .heif):
what iPhones and many other phones and cameras save. 8 and 10-bit
photos, photos stored in tiles, turned and mirrored photos, and Display
P3 colour (converted to sRGB) all work. HEIF files with AV1 inside
(AVIF) and HEIF image sequences aren't read.

It is a small program, LumenHEIF, which Lumen runs in the background for
each HEIF photo it needs: for a thumbnail it takes the photo's own small
thumbnail (quick); for the viewer and exports it decodes the photo.
Decoding uses NEON when the processor has it.

It lives in Lumen's Plugins directory (!Lumen.Plugins.HEIF); PackMan
puts it there, or drag the HEIF directory from the zip into Lumen's
Plug-ins > Add plug-in window (it works at once), or it is found the
next time Lumen starts. It is a format plug-in: its Plugin file tells
Lumen which files are HEIF photos, so it needs Lumen 0.0.37 or later.
HEIF photos are imported once it is there.

A 12 megapixel photo needs about 100 MB of memory while it is decoded.

